SC&D Assignment #02: Refactoring Order Billing Engine

Overview

This repository contains the complete refactoring solution for Assignment 2 in Software Construction & Design (SC&D). The objective of this project is to safely renovate a legacy, monolithic OrderBillingEngine system by implementing an automated JUnit 5 testing safety net, performing a thorough Code Smell and SOLID audit, and applying modern design patterns to achieve a clean, modular architecture.

Project Structure & Implementation Details

src/
└── assignment2/
    ├── task1/
    │   ├── OrderBillingEngine.java
    │   └── OrderBillingEngineTest.java
    └── task2/
        ├── Task2Runner.java
        ├── domain/
        │   ├── Order.java
        │   └── Product.java
        ├── calculator/
        │   ├── TaxCalculator.java
        │   └── DiscountCalculator.java
        ├── payment/
        │   ├── PaymentStrategy.java
        │   ├── CreditCardPayment.java
        │   ├── PaypalPayment.java
        │   └── BitcoinPayment.java
        ├── notification/
        │   ├── NotificationDispatcher.java
        │   ├── EmailNotificationDispatcher.java
        │   └── SmsNotificationDispatcher.java
        └── repository/
            ├── OrderRepository.java
            └── FileOrderRepository.java


Task 1: Legacy Code Safety Net (JUnit 5 Testing)

Location: assignment2.task1

Contents: 01 Java Class (OrderBillingEngine.java) and 01 JUnit 5 Test Suite (OrderBillingEngineTest.java).

Details: Before refactoring, a comprehensive characterization test suite was constructed to cover all legacy edge cases. The test suite verifies discounts, tax calculations, payment methods, invalid inputs, and error paths, achieving a 100% pass rate with 0 failures to ensure zero regression during refactoring.

Task 2 & 3: Code Smell Audit & Clean Architecture Redesign

Location: assignment2.task2

Contents: 14 Java Classes designed to modularize the legacy monolithic engine.

Architecture Breakdown:

Domain Layer: Order and Product model classes representing core business data.

Calculators: Decoupled TaxCalculator and DiscountCalculator handling specific monetary computations.

Payment Strategy Pattern: PaymentStrategy interface implemented by CreditCardPayment, PaypalPayment, and BitcoinPayment to eliminate nested if-else conditionals.

Notification Dispatchers: NotificationDispatcher interface implemented by EmailNotificationDispatcher and SmsNotificationDispatcher for decoupled communications.

Repository Pattern: OrderRepository interface and FileOrderRepository implementation to isolate persistence mechanisms.

Execution: Task2Runner.java serves as the driver class executing the clean, refactored workflow.

Task 4: Step-by-Step Git Commit Trail

Details: The refactoring process was conducted through disciplined, incremental commits rather than bulk uploads. The Git log contains 10 logical commits tracking the step-by-step progress from baseline setup to final architecture verification.

Technical Constraints & Compatibility

Java Collection Handling: Strict implementation of raw-type collection structures to guarantee seamless cross-environment compilation and IDE rendering.

Testing Framework: JUnit 5 (Jupiter engine).

Design Principles Applied: Single Responsibility Principle (SRP), Open/Closed Principle (OCP), Dependency Inversion Principle (DIP), Strategy Pattern, and Repository Pattern.

How to Run the Project

Clone the Repository:

git clone <YOUR_REPOSITORY_LINK>
cd <REPOSITORY_FOLDER>


Execute Unit Tests (Task 1):
Run OrderBillingEngineTest.java within your IDE or standard build tool to confirm the 100% test pass rate.

Run Refactored Architecture (Task 2/3):
Execute Task2Runner.java to verify the execution of the refactored billing engine.

Verify Commit Trail (Task 4):

git log --oneline
